```jsx
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const Autocomplete = ({ data, placeholder, onSelect }) => {
  const [suggestions, setSuggestions] = useState([]);
  const [inputValue, setInputValue] = useState('');
  const [showSuggestions, setShowSuggestions] = useState(false);
  const timeout = null;

  const handleChange = (event) => {
    const value = event.target.value;
    setInputValue(value);

    if (value.length > 0) {
      if (timeout) {
        clearTimeout(timeout);
      }
      timeout = setTimeout(() => {
        const suggestions = data.filter((item) => item.toLowerCase().indexOf(value.toLowerCase()) > -1);
        setSuggestions(suggestions);
        setShowSuggestions(true);
      }, 500);
    } else {
      setSuggestions([]);
      setShowSuggestions(false);
    }
  };

  const handleSelection = (event, suggestion) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    onSelect(suggestion);
    setInputValue(suggestion);
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <input
        type="text"
        value={inputValue}
        onChange={handleChange}
        placeholder={placeholder}
      />
      {showSuggestions && (
        <ul>
          {suggestions.map((suggestion, index) => (
            <li key={index} onClick={(event) => handleSelection(event, suggestion)}>
              {suggestion}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      )}
    </div>
  );
};

export default Autocomplete;
```

In this component:

*   We maintain four states: `suggestions`, `inputValue`, `showSuggestions` and `timeout`. Each state is an important part of the autocomplete functionality.
*   When the user inputs something, we use `setTimeout` to wait for 500ms (or a specified timeout) and then filter the data based on the user's input. This allows users to type in a sequence of characters before we start providing suggestions.
*   We keep track of whether any suggestions are displayed using the `showSuggestions` state variable. When this state is true, we display the suggestions list below the input field.
*   When a user selects a suggestion, we call the `onSelect` callback function with the selected suggestion as the argument.<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>

